-# FH6 Radio Tool v3.0.33
+# FH6 Radio Tool v3.0.34 Hotfix
 
-## Main-menu music workflow simplification
-
-- Changed the main-menu / press-start music replacement workflow to use the known FH6 bank automatically: `GLB_RadioPressStart.assets.bank`.
-- Users no longer need to manually choose or auto-detect the menu music bank.
-- Users only need to select the replacement audio file; the tool resolves the bank from the selected game root / `media/Audio/FMODBanks` directory.
-- The workflow replaces the single music entry in that bank, then generates a package or performs one-click replacement with backup.
-- Radio station replacement and RadioInfo XML patching remain separate and unchanged.
-
-## Previous v3 fixes kept
-
-- Keeps the v3.0.31 manifest fix for `rebuilt_files` in package-only workflows.
-- Keeps the Nuitka build workflow and Nexus-oriented source/package layout.
+- Fixed the v3.0.33 portable EXE prompt that incorrectly told users to run `setup_env.bat` for missing `pywinauto`.
+- In the Nexus/Nuitka EXE package, `setup_env.bat` is intentionally not present; running an old v2 setup script cannot repair a compiled EXE.
+- The Nuitka builder now verifies Windows automation dependencies before building and includes `pywinauto`, `comtypes`, `win32com`, and Win32 modules more explicitly.
+- The Nexus package builder no longer copies a separate `ffmpeg.exe` into the final upload ZIP by default.
+- Main-menu music replacement remains fixed to `GLB_RadioPressStart.assets.bank`; users only select the replacement audio.
